  "notes": "ウザい is slang for \"annoying\" or \"irritating,\" derived from ⟦{鬱陶|うっとう}しい→鬱陶しい：06169_uttoushii⟧.\n\nFORMS (i-adjective):\n- Negative: ウザく⟦ない→ない：01118_nai⟧\n- Past: ウザかった\n- Adverb: ウザく\n\nWRITING:\nUsually written in katakana (ウザい) or hiragana (うざい). The katakana emphasizes the slang nature.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/slang and can be rude when directed at people. Common among younger speakers. Avoid in formal situations.\n\nSIMILAR SLANG:\n- ⟦キモい→キモい：04754_kimoi⟧: gross, creepy\n- ⟦ダルい→だるい：05307_darui⟧: tiresome, sluggish\n- ⟦ウケる→受ける：01215_ukeru⟧: hilarious (positive)\n\nFORMS:\nウザっ (interjection): Ugh! Annoying!",
